WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.422
Picture a case note that says, "Family resistant. Refused two

00:00:03.422 --> 00:00:06.844
contact attempts." It reads like a fact. It is actually

00:00:06.844 --> 00:00:10.267
a story about character, built from two missed calls. Psychologists

00:00:10.267 --> 00:00:13.689
have studied this kind of story for decades. People lean

00:00:13.689 --> 00:00:17.111
toward explaining behavior by who someone is, even when the

00:00:17.111 --> 00:00:18.480
situation explains it well.

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:22.230
Here is why it happens to good, careful people. Judging

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:25.630
another person runs in three quick steps. First, you notice

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:29.030
what they did. Second, you infer a trait. Third, you

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:32.430
correct for the situation. The first two steps are fast

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:35.830
and nearly automatic. The third takes effort. In a classic

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:39.230
set of experiments, people who were mentally busy skipped that

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:41.950
third step. People who could focus made it.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:46.071
A full queue or a stack of renewals is exactly

00:00:46.071 --> 00:00:47.580
that kind of busy.

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:51.622
So what helps? Many trainings say to put yourself in

00:00:51.622 --> 00:00:55.315
the other person's shoes. Researchers tested that advice across 25

00:00:55.315 --> 00:00:59.007
experiments. Imagining the other view did not reliably improve accuracy.

00:00:59.007 --> 00:01:02.699
Sometimes it lowered accuracy while raising confidence. What worked was

00:01:02.699 --> 00:01:06.392
asking. In the final study, people who asked their partner

00:01:06.392 --> 00:01:10.084
first got more than twice as many predictions exactly right

00:01:10.084 --> 00:01:11.930
as people who only imagined.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:15.934
That points to a simple method, first taught at the

00:01:15.934 --> 00:01:19.587
University of Minnesota in the 1970s. Describe, Interpret, Evaluate. Describe

00:01:19.587 --> 00:01:23.241
what a camera could confirm. Two calls, both at ten

00:01:23.241 --> 00:01:26.895
in the morning on weekdays. Voicemails left in English. A

00:01:26.895 --> 00:01:30.549
file that lists a different primary language. Then interpret, with

00:01:30.549 --> 00:01:34.202
more than one possible meaning. Maybe the family works mornings.

00:01:34.202 --> 00:01:36.760
Maybe they could not understand the message.

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:40.310
Maybe they did not know who was calling. Only then

00:01:40.310 --> 00:01:42.870
evaluate, and hold that evaluation open to correction.

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:46.607
Notice that the best explanations in that list were about

00:01:46.607 --> 00:01:49.993
the process, not the family. Those are the facts busy

00:01:49.993 --> 00:01:53.380
minds skip. They are also the facts you can change.

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:56.947
Then ask. Use a qualified interpreter. Offer a few times

00:01:56.947 --> 00:02:00.164
and channels. Say what will happen with the answer. Asking

00:02:00.164 --> 00:02:03.381
someone who depends on you for services takes care, because

00:02:03.381 --> 00:02:06.598
power can make a yes mean very little. A private

00:02:06.598 --> 00:02:08.850
way to correct the record later helps.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:12.928
Be honest about the evidence. The research on attribution is

00:02:12.928 --> 00:02:16.655
strong, but much of it comes from laboratory studies. No

00:02:16.655 --> 00:02:20.383
controlled study was found that shows the three-step method itself

00:02:20.383 --> 00:02:24.111
changes workplace outcomes. Its parts rest on firmer ground: describe

00:02:24.111 --> 00:02:26.720
first, check the situation, and ask directly.

00:02:27.070 --> 00:02:29.699
As a leader, you can make this normal for your

00:02:29.699 --> 00:02:32.327
team. Ask for the observation before the assessment. Treat a

00:02:32.327 --> 00:02:34.956
judgment word as a cue to ask what was seen.

00:02:34.956 --> 00:02:37.584
Thank the person who brings back a fact that changes

00:02:37.584 --> 00:02:40.213
the plan. The next time a quick story forms in

00:02:40.213 --> 00:02:42.841
your mind, find the one fact you are missing, and

00:02:42.841 --> 00:02:43.630
go get it.
